		(uuid "b3fe7236-040b-5554-9872-b29dabe987e4")
	)
	(text "Q3 orientation: the drain faces J3 and the source is +5V, so the body diode\nconducts on a correct supply and the gate at GND turns the channel on.\nReversed, the body diode blocks and Vgs stays 0 V: Q3 stays off."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 17.78 81.28 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "ee2c6ea2-2216-5f26-a2e8-4f3c3b62254f")
	)
	(text "D2 clamps Vgs near -6.2 V. R1 limits D2's current and discharges the gate.\nD1 sits after Q3: it takes short spikes, never a reversed supply."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 17.78 88.9 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "e40ab826-5541-534c-9f32-a8805c74cb20")
	)
	(text "J3 and the Pi's USB power port feed the same +5V rail: never both at once.\nA 9 V or 12 V adapter on J3 damages the Pi and M1 in seconds: the board has\nno overvoltage protection. Silkscreen at J3: REGULATED 5 V IN. NO USB CABLE ON THE PI."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 17.78 111.76 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "4d79efb6-3c7f-5e5e-8d4c-294a6a581784")
	)
	(text "To verify: Q3 SOT-23 pads 1 gate, 2 source, 3 drain, as the AO3401A and\nDMG2305UX (from memory, common but not universal). Own symbol Q_PMOS_GSD_SOT23.\nD1 P6KE6.8A DO-15 pads 1 cathode, 2 anode. F1 uses the 1.1 A class outline,\nbody 10.0 x 3.5 mm, leads 5.1 mm apart, drill 1.0 mm: an MF-R090 is larger\nthan an MF-R020 and fits inside it. All dimensions and parts from memory."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 17.78 134.62 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "79fc499b-4f08-5069-aa32-f02a21108b22")
	)
